From: Brad Nicholas <70774+bradn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 08:53:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Join README HTML rows on iOS; let tall inline images open
 their line

HTML <p> and heading blocks written one element per source line now read
as one line in the iOS reader, as on GitHub: HardWrapReflow gains an HTML
join (a break between visible content shows as one space; breaks around
tag-only lines show as nothing). README badge rows sit side by side and
the gaps around them close. The Mac passes joinsHTMLParagraphs: false,
so its rendering is unchanged.

Inside a joined paragraph every image is inline, and <img width/height>
are honoured. A picture taller than its line raises the paragraph's
minimum line height (MarkdownContentStorage.fittingInlineImages):
TextKit ignores an attachment's height when only zero-width characters
follow it, which hidden </a></p> become. Only inline images carry the new
drInlineImageHeight attribute, so text and inline math are unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
